ers, where did 20s come from?\"]],[null,[null,0,\"In gemini_webapi, there are two separate timeouts interacting:\",[[3,16,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"The HTTP / transport timeout: Default client initialization (client.init(...) or CLI defaults) frequently sets short connection/read timeouts (e.g. 20s or 30s).\",[[0,29,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[61,77,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"The stall threshold calculation:\",[[0,32,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,null,null,[\"stall_threshold \\u003d min(self.timeout, self.watchdog_timeout)\\n\",\"python\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"If self.timeout (or the underlying transport read timeout) evaluates to ~20–30s while self.watchdog_timeout is 120s, min() clamps the threshold down to 20 seconds.\",[[3,15,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[86,107,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[117,122,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[152,162,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Because is_thinking initializes to False, the stream loop treats the initial silence during reasoning as an unestablished or stalled stream, falling back directly to that lower clamp.\",[[8,19,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[35,40,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]]]]]]]]]],1]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"3. How to address his comment directly\"]],[null,[null,0,\"You don't need to argue over who configured what\"]]]]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,\"3.8 Flash\",true,[[[[1004,\"Longer\",5,null,[\"expand\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/expand/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1005,\"Shorter\",6,null,[\"compress\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/compress/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1003,\"Personalize\",3,null,[\"personal_recommendati