why luuquangvu responded the way he did, and where the 20-second vs. 120-second discrepancy comes from:\",[[29,39,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"1. Who is luuquangvu and why does he think it's 120s / 450s?\",[[10,20,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"luuquangvu is the core contributor who authored the streaming performance, zombie stream retry logic, and extended thinking pull requests (PR #220, PR #237, PR #310) in HanaokaYuzu/Gemini-API.\",[[0,10,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[169,191,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"In his implementation of the streaming retry and watchdog lifecycle:\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"Default overall request / session stream timeout: 450s.\",[[0,49,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Default stream watchdog / zombie stall timeout: 120s.\",[[0,47,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"Because he authored those numbers, in his mind the watchdog is hardcoded or defaulted to wait 120 seconds before deciding a stream has stalled. When he saw your log:\",[[94,105,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,null,null,[\"[Watchdog] Socket idle for 20s. Refreshing connection...\\n\",\"\"]],[null,[null,0,\"he immediately assumed:\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[null,[null,0,\"\\\"Wait, if my watchdog default is 120s, why on earth did your socket abort after only 20 seconds? You must have passed a 20s watchdog setting or broken configuration.\\\"\",[[0,166,[[null,null,null,null,1]]]]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"2. If you didn't customize any timers, where did 20s come from?\"]],[null,[null,0,\"In gemini_webapi, there are two separate timeouts interacting:\",[[3,16,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"The HTTP / transport timeout: Default client initialization (client.init(...) or CLI defaults) frequently sets short connection/read timeouts (e.g. 20s or 30s).\",[[0,29,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[61,77,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[30,160,[null,null,null,[null,[\"spp_d1ae00196c4b86\"]]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"The stall threshold calculation:\",[[0,32,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,null,null,[\"stall_threshold \\u003d min(self.timeout, self.watchdog_timeout)\\n\",\"python\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"If self.timeout (or the underlying transport read timeout) evaluates to ~20–30s while self.watchdog_timeout is 120s, min() clamps the threshold down to 20 seconds.\",[[3,15,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[86,107,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[117,122,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[152,162,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Because is_thinking initializes to False, the stream loop treats the initial silence during reasoning as an unestablished or stalled stream, falling back directly to that lower clamp.\",[[8,19,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[35,40,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]]]]]]]]]],1]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"3. How to address his comment directly\"]],[null,[null,0,\"You don't need to argue over who configured what—point out that under default client settings, stall_threshold \\u003d min(self.timeout, self.watchdog_timeout) evaluates to the transport timeout when no chunks have arrived yet:\",[[95,153,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,null,null,[\"@luuquangvu No custom timers were set—the 20s comes from the default transport timeout clamp:\\n\\nDuring the initial reasoning phase, because `is_thinking` starts as `False`, `stall_threshold` evaluates to `min(self.timeout, self.watchdog_timeout)`. Even with `watchdog_timeout\\u003d120`, if the underlying socket read/transport timeout evaluates lower (or during initial chunk wait), the watchdog flags socket inactivity before the first token delta arrives.\\n\\nInitializing `is_thinking \\u003d True if extended_thinking else False` avoids mistaking the model's pre-token reasoning time for a stalled stream and lets it await the first candidate chunk.\\n\",\"markdown\"]]]]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,\"3.8 Flash\",true,[[[[1004,\"Longer\",5,null,[\"expand\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/expand/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1005,\"Shorter\",6,null,[\"compress\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/compress/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1003,\"Personalize\",3,null,[\"personal_recommendations\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/personal_recommendations/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1001,\"Try again\",1,null,[\"refresh\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/refresh/default/24px.svg\",null,true]]]]],null,2,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,null,3,null,[[1,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[4,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[6,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[15,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[20,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[22,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[23,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[3,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[5,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[7,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[9,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[21,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[35,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[42,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[14,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[17,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[2,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[8,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[10,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[11,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[12,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[13,[1791164727,782159000],1,null,[1]],[